        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, an asphalt shingle roof typically costs between $8,500 and $18,000 for standard residential installation, whereas a metal roof ranges from $20,000 to $40,000+ depending on the system. While asphalt has a lower initial price, metal provides superior longevity and performance against heavy mountain snow and high winds.",
